MathCAT (en rules): accents read with "start" and "end"

A rule for the accent intents Mathessible gives `x\bar`, `x\vec`, `x\hat`
and the other accents (src/mathessible/mathcat/prepare.py, `_accents`):
intent="bar:accent($base)", the accent's name then the property. It reads
"start bar, x y z t, end bar", so what an accent covers is heard: MathCAT
read `xyzt\bar` (the bar over t) and `(xyzt)\bar` (over all four) both
"x y z t bar", and an accent over an expression "quantity a plus b with
line above", with no end.

Applied by scripts/bootstrap.sh on top of upstream 85c89a37 (the rule at the
end of the file, away from 0003's context lines). Mathessible's own; the other languages'
rules do not have it yet (they read "bar of t").

diff --git a/Rules/Languages/en/SharedRules/general.yaml b/Rules/Languages/en/SharedRules/general.yaml
--- a/Rules/Languages/en/SharedRules/general.yaml
+++ b/Rules/Languages/en/SharedRules/general.yaml
@@ -1104,3 +1104,18 @@
   match: "."
   replace:
   - x: "*"
+
+# Mathessible: an accent over (or under) its base, given by Mathessible as intent="bar:accent($base)" (the
+# accent's name, then the property): "start bar, x y z t, end bar", so what the accent covers is heard.
+# At the end of the file, away from patch 0003's context lines.
+- name: accent
+  tag: "*"
+  match: "count(*)=1 and contains(@data-intent-property, ':accent:')"
+  replace:
+  - t: "start"      # phrase('start' bar, x, end bar)
+  - x: "SpeakIntentName(name(.), $Verbosity, 'nofix')"
+  - pause: short
+  - x: "*[1]"
+  - pause: short
+  - t: "end"      # phrase(start bar, x, 'end' bar)
+  - x: "SpeakIntentName(name(.), $Verbosity, 'nofix')"
